This book offers the first annotated German translation of the Syrian Life of Mor Gabriel. The author, himself a native of Beth Qustan, has based his work on a thorough study of the sources. He takes into account oral as well as literary traditions and subjects contradictory reports to historical criticism. Many illustrations of the monastery and the original manuscripts complete the work</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
